~ how_do_I_locate_tuf
Sky: Connect this frequency: 543.210 sf1[do sky.cooldown_words.append("triangulator_freq_given")][next=auto]
Sky: It will connect you to a remote terminal which then will allow you to [url=FreeDictionaryTriangulation][u]triangulate[/u][/url] the location of a frequency.
- How does this work
	~ how_does_tria_works
	do sky.cooldown_words.append("how does tria works asked")
	if GameState.plugin_bitmap_installed == 2:
		do Global.create_empty_lines("Sky",false)
		[font_size=25]|---------- [pulse]Loading Image[/pulse] ----------|[/font_size][do Global.create_image("Sky", "tria_guide.png", true, Vector2(369, 275))][next=auto]
		[speed=5][font_size=25]|___________________________________|[/font_size][next=auto]
		do Global.create_empty_lines("Sky",true)
	else:
		Computer: [color=#FF5555]err: invalid_parser//[/color] bitmap_map=7dofkpkuafvbkvdusvhkpa.img
	Sky: ">6" in the image is your reciever spot. number shows the distance. it is 6 units away from the transmission.[next=auto]
	Sky: You will have 3 spots. Blinking spot is the one which will move next.[next=auto]
- what is triangulation
	Sky: If you listen a radiowave from 3 different spots, in the shape of a triangle, then narrow that triangle to the edge where reception is the highest, you can find its location.[next=auto]
	Sky: Assuming you do the narrowing step multiple times.
	- How does triangulator work [if sky.cooldown_words.has("how does tria works asked") == false]
		=> how_does_tria_works
	- got it

Sky: In triangulator type "set tuf 331.453 sf1"[next=auto]
Sky: It is the frequency conference servers are communicating to one another.[wait=0.5] Once you locate, you'll transmit reverse frequency to noise cancel it, it should mess up the server side sync.[next=auto]
=> END

